# <%= name %>

A BUSY Bar app written in Python. Replace this line with what it shows.

## Owns

- What the app draws (`src/<%= moduleName %>/render.py`) and how often it
  redraws (`src/<%= moduleName %>/__main__.py`).

## Does not own

- Connection settings, the frame loop, and shutdown handling. Those live in
  [`bar-kit-py`](<%= offset %>libs/bar-kit-py/README.md).

## Start here

- `src/<%= moduleName %>/render.py`: maps a moment in time to display
  elements. Keep it pure so tests can pin the time.
- `src/<%= moduleName %>/__main__.py`: hands `render` to `run_bar_app`.
- `src/<%= moduleName %>/preview.py`: sample frames for the app catalogue
  ([tools/catalogue](<%= offset %>tools/catalogue/README.md)).

## Run

Set `BUSYBAR_ADDR` and `BUSYBAR_TOKEN` in `.env.local` if the bar is not
plugged in over USB (see [docs/busy-bar.md](<%= offset %>docs/busy-bar.md)), then:

```sh
NX_DAEMON=false yarn nx run <%= name %>:start
```

## Verify

```sh
NX_DAEMON=false yarn nx run-many -t lint typecheck test -p <%= name %>
```
